From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rhys Perry <pendingchaos02@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:49:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aco/ra: check next register against bounds in subdword
 get_reg_simple path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes eventual assertion failure with GFX10.3 and
dEQP-VK.ray_tracing_pipeline.misc.shaderRecordExplicitSTD430Offset_6.

Signed-off-by: Rhys Perry <pendingchaos02@gmail.com>
Backport-to: *
Reviewed-by: Daniel Schürmann <daniel@schuermann.dev>
(cherry picked from commit f9a2d34a19c496e552b6cd603e7807f1025a2e98)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44820>
(cherry picked from commit a1254bb164e72c4bc3509458954c83c69fcdf4fd)
---
 src/amd/compiler/aco_register_allocation.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/compiler/aco_register_allocation.cpp b/src/amd/compiler/aco_register_allocation.cpp
index 8acc8819922..50bf1bc1550 100644
--- a/src/amd/compiler/aco_register_allocation.cpp
+++ b/src/amd/compiler/aco_register_allocation.cpp
@@ -1032,8 +1032,10 @@ get_reg_simple(ra_ctx& ctx, const RegisterFile& reg_file, DefInfo info,
                            [](unsigned v) { return v == 0; });
 
             /* check if also the neighboring reg is free if needed */
-            if (reg_found && i + rc.bytes() > 4)
-               reg_found = (reg_file[PhysReg{entry.first + 1}] == 0);
+            if (reg_found && i + rc.bytes() > 4) {
+               PhysReg next = PhysReg{entry.first + 1};
+               reg_found = next < bounds.end().reg && reg_file[next] == 0;
+            }
 
             if (reg_found) {
                PhysReg res{entry.first};
-- 
